    "body": "## What changed\n- require a persisted authenticated user id before all user-facing Stripe Connect onboarding status, refresh and link operations\n- reuse the verified actor id for payout-recipient and locked-user reads\n- reject missing or transient principals before payout repositories, identity verification, user state or Stripe gateway access\n- add regression coverage asserting zero financial/provider interactions for invalid principals\n- document the payout-onboarding identity invariant\n\n## Security / financial rationale\nStripe Connect onboarding reads and provisions payout-recipient state. Missing or transient principals must fail closed before any financial persistence, provider-side access or external payout-account provisioning.\n\n## Validation\nExact-head GitHub Actions must be green before merge. Merge only with the validated head SHA and a merge commit.",
